{
  "_comment": [
    "Demo teachers, for a working app on a fresh clone. These people are invented — the names, the",
    "subject allocations and the hours are all made up, and none of it describes anyone real. The",
    "subject codes are the ones in ../courses.json so that a seeded database can actually produce a",
    "timetable.",
    "",
    "This replaces the campus.sqlite3 that used to be committed. That file held real, named",
    "academics with their teaching loads and weekly working hours, which is not something to keep in",
    "a repository with a public remote; JSON also has the advantage of being reviewable in a diff,",
    "which a binary database is not.",
    "",
    "Load it with:  dotnet run --project src/RoutinePlanner.Web -- --seed",
    "It refuses to run if the teachers table already has rows, unless you add --force."
  ],
